# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .easignore — files EXCLUDED from EAS Build upload
# Only app/, src/, assets/, and config files get uploaded.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Private keys
keys/
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.jks
*.mobileprovision

# Reference docs / plans / design docs (not app code)
plans/
_elevate_audit/
design-system/
scripts/
app-audit/
logo-concepts/
supabase/

# Markdown / text reference files
*.md
!node_modules/**/*.md

# Screenshots / design mockups at root
emulator-*.png

# Native projects — MUST be excluded.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the EAS upload. android/ and ios/ are
# gitignored (they are prebuild output), but they were not listed here, so they
# were uploaded — and EAS skips `expo prebuild` when native directories are
# present. Builds were made from whatever prebuild output happened to be on
# this machine.
#
# That silently dropped health.WRITE_WEIGHT from build 40: it was added to
# app.json on 2026-08-24, while the uploaded AndroidManifest.xml had been
# generated on 2026-08-08 and was never regenerated. targetSdk 36 and the
# Health Connect crash fix survived only because gradle.properties and
# MainActivity.kt had been patched on this machine too.
#
# The failure mode is the dangerous one: app.json is edited, the build succeeds,
# and the change is simply absent. Excluding these makes EAS regenerate them
# from app.json and the config plugins on every build.
/android
/ios

# Dist / build artifacts (rebuilt on server)
dist/
web-build/

# Dev tooling
.expo/
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# Tester feedback / misc text
tester-feedback.md
JAMIES-DESIGN-IDEAS.md
PAGE-REFERENCE.md

# Misc files not needed for build
.env.example
.mcp.json
tsc.log
